<title>SWEDEN: Scania Q1 profit almost halved.</title>
<headline>Scania Q1 profit almost halved.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish truck maker Scania released the following figures for the first three months of 1997, ending March 31.</p>
<p>					  (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		   577  vs 1,113</p>
<p> Sales					8,804  vs 8,726</p>
<p> Earnings per share (crowns)	    2.10 vs 3.95</p>
<p> Operating costs			 6,778   vs 6,275</p>
<p> Operating income			  642   vs 1,229</p>
<p> Net financial items	     CHARGE 65   vs   116 CHARGE</p>
<p> Share of associated companies	  81   vs    91</p>
<p> Taxes					 157   vs   321</p>
<p> Net income				  420   vs   792</p>
<p>NOTE -- Analysts had forecast a 608 million crown profit after financial items.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
